   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Culinary and courtesy",
   "texto": [
    "To express that something you like in Dutch is not usually used a verb equivalent to «gustar», but «lekker vinden» (literally «parecerte rico»): «Ik vind de soep lekker» (I like soup). In questions: «Vindt u de soep lekker?» (Do you like soup?). To order courteously in a restaurant is used «Ik wil graag...» (I would like... / I would like...): «Ik wil graag soep»."
   ]
